      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-3z &=-8 \\\\ y+z &=5 \\\\ z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=R_{2}-R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}+3R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-2R_{2},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=7 \\\\ y &=0 \\\\ z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=7$, $y=0$, and $z=5$.",
